
To install gem5, please follow these steps:

1) Clone the repository including all the submodules,
	for that use the "--recursive" option as show below:

	git clone --recursive https://gite.lirmm.fr/gem5/gem5.git

	If you don't have the rights, please contact maintainers.


2) Check the gcc version.

	In order to compile Ramulator, gcc 7 is needed at least.
	You can check gcc version using the following command:

	gcc --version

	If you want to compile on jaguar, please check the gcc version.
	By default the version 4 is used. For switching to version 7,
	you can use the next command:

	scl enable devtoolset-7 bash


3) Compile the project using Scons.

	For ARM architecture:
	scons ./build/ARM/gem5.opt

	For X86 architecture:
	scons ./build/X86/gem5.opt

	You can use the -jN to allow parallel compilation on N cores 
	
	Also, you can read the tutorial above for more details on building gem5:
	http://learning.gem5.org/book/part1/building.html 


5) Usual errors:

	- If you already clone gem5 and you didn't include the submodules,
		run the following command:

		git submodule update --init

		You can check if the folders ./simpoint and ./ext/ramulator/Ramulator
		are empty or not. 





